      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-121471",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/e6/e6a38f5b59c17e5e65f0ab0c0829aa9a0b628e1a0a5cd4851c71a9d61b8d4496.png)\n\nConsider the graph above, where the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are defined as\n$f(x) =-e^{x/3}, g(x) = 3^{x} - 3.3$.\n\nBy creating a table of values, find, to one decimal place, a solution to the equation $f(x) = g(x)$.\n\n*Hint: $e \\approx 2.718282$ is Euler's Number.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
