      ":question/problem": "![](images/21/21ea060a7d7e07c9a6f2496a6a9767fa21af193ce2505ffe6c53d31a82460136.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are defined as\n\n$f(x) = \\mid x^{2} - 1 \\mid, g(x) =-\\frac{1}{2}x + \\frac{9}{4}$.\n\nBy creating a table of values, find, to one decimal place, a solution to the equation $f(x) = g(x)$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
